{"name":"Blue Phlox","hex":"#d2e6e8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"phlox","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any flowering plant of the genus Phlox."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phlox"}],"entries":[{"title":"Phlox divaricata","blocks":[{"text":"Phlox divaricata, the wild blue phlox, woodland phlox, or wild sweet william, is a species of flowering plant in the family Polemoniaceae, native to forests and fields in eastern North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Phlox_divaricata_Ohio_2016.JPG/330px-Phlox_divaricata_Ohio_2016.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phlox_divaricata"},{"title":"Phlox","blocks":[{"text":"Phlox is a genus of 68 species of perennial and annual plants in the family Polemoniaceae. They are found mostly in North America in diverse habitats from alpine tundra to open woodland and prairie. Some flower in spring, others in summer and fall. Flowers may be pale blue, violet, pink, bright red, or white. Many are fragrant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Phlox_glaberrima.jpg/330px-Phlox_glaberrima.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phlox"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on 